---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../../site.config.mjs';
---
<Base
  title="About"
  description={`About ${site.name}: who publishes it, how articles are researched and sourced, and our disclosure policy.`}
>
  <article class="post prose">
    <h1>About {site.name}</h1>
    <p>
      {site.name} is a technology publication covering AI models, tokens, developer tooling,
      open-weight models, and agent workflows. Our goal is to explain these topics clearly for
      builders who ship software, evaluate models, and run AI systems.
    </p>

    <h2>Who publishes this site</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>{site.name} is published by the team behind <a href="https://onlyorders.tech">OnlyOrders</a></strong>,
      a multi-channel AI auto-reply and chat-order platform for online sellers. We are an
      educational content project run by that team — we are not an independent journalism outlet.
      When an article mentions {site.publisher.name}, it carries a disclosure note.
    </p>

    <h2>How we write</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Every article lists its sources, preferring primary sources such as official announcements, research posts, and security advisories.</li>
      <li>We use AI tools to help with research and drafting. A human reviews claims against the sources before publishing.</li>
      <li>We do not invent benchmarks, prices, statistics, or product capabilities. Vendor claims are attributed to the vendor.</li>
      <li>Where a topic is speculative or lacks a reliable public source, we say so and frame it as analysis rather than fact.</li>
      <li>Corrections: if you spot an error, contact the {site.publisher.name} team via <a href={site.publisher.url}>{site.publisher.url}</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Base>
